:: Octavia \[Event\] - Two Camps One Chief [bg-guesthouse]
<h1 class="ptitle">OCTAVIA</h1>
<br />
<<set $characters.octavia.quests.two_camps_day = $game.day>>

You're barely through the door when boots hit the path outside — too fast, too hard to be anything good.
<br /><br />
<center>
    <<image 'people/octavia/two_camps1.jpg'>>
</center>
<br />
<<newgirl>>
<<set _messenger = $tmpGirl>>
The door bangs open. One of Octavia's warriors, chest heaving, a fresh cut over one eyebrow, blood not all her own.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _messenger>>
    White faction. A column of them, moving on the Emberclaw camp. We spotted them an hour out — maybe less by now.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
Octavia is already reaching for her blades before the warrior finishes talking. Then the settlement's own horn sounds — low, urgent, three long blasts. Someone else is at your gate.
<br /><br />
<center>
    <<image 'people/octavia/two_camps2.jpg'>>
</center>
<br />
Octavia freezes for half a second — the only half-second of hesitation you've ever seen from her.
<br /><br />
<<octavia>>
    They timed it. Of course they timed it.
<</octavia>>
<br />
<<octavia>>
    I can't be in two places. Neither can you. So we decide — now.
<</octavia>>
<br />

<div id="option_emberclaw">
    <<linkreplace 'Ride to Emberclaw with her — the settlement holds itself'>>
        <<set $characters.octavia.quests.two_camps_choice = 'emberclaw'>>
        <<run $('#option_settlement').hide()>>
        <<run $('#option_split').hide()>>
        <<octavia>>
            With me, then. Emberclaw needs numbers more than your walls need you tonight.
        <</octavia>>
        <br /><br />
        <<link 'Ride out'>>
            <<addhours 1>>
            <<goto 'Octavia [Event] - Two Camps One Chief - Emberclaw Fight'>>
        <</link>>
    <</linkreplace>>
</div>
<div id="option_settlement">
    <<linkreplace 'Send her back alone — you hold the settlement'>>
        <<set $characters.octavia.quests.two_camps_choice = 'settlement'>>
        <<run $('#option_emberclaw').hide()>>
        <<run $('#option_split').hide()>>
        <<octavia>>
            Your call. I'll take what I've got and go. Don't die here while I'm not looking.
        <</octavia>>
        <br /><br />
        She's out the door before you can answer, warrior at her heels.
        <br /><br />
        <<link 'Turn to the settlement's defense'>>
            <<addhours 1>>
            <<goto 'Octavia [Event] - Two Camps One Chief - Settlement Fight'>>
        <</link>>
    <</linkreplace>>
</div>
<div id="option_split">
    <<if Object.keys($player.companions ?? {}).length >= 2>>
        <<linkreplace 'Split the forces — send companions with her, hold the settlement yourself'>>
            <<set $characters.octavia.quests.two_camps_choice = 'split'>>
            <<run $('#option_emberclaw').hide()>>
            <<run $('#option_settlement').hide()>>
            <<octavia>>
                Half measures get people killed. But... it might be enough. Give me what you can spare.
            <</octavia>>
            <br /><br />
            <<link 'Send them with her'>>
                <<addhours 1>>
                <<goto 'Octavia [Event] - Two Camps One Chief - Split Fight'>>
            <</link>>
        <</linkreplace>>
    <<else>>
        <div class="link-internal disabled" style="background: #ccc">
            Split the forces (need at least 2 companions)
        </div>
    <</if>>
</div>
